# Keep the build context small and reproducible. Anything listed here is never
# sent to the Docker daemon, so a stale local bin/ can't leak into the image.
#
# IMPORTANT: patterns are matched against paths relative to the CONTEXT ROOT and are NOT
# recursive. A bare "appsettings.json" matches ONLY ./appsettings.json — it does not match
# src/InvitationPlatform.Api/appsettings.json. Anything that can appear at any depth needs
# an explicit "**/" prefix, which is why every entry below is written that way.
bin/
obj/
out/
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/

# Local IDE / user state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# Never bake secrets or user content into an image.
#
# appsettings.json is excluded deliberately: developers fill their local copy with real
# credentials, and anything copied into a layer stays in the image even if a later layer
# deletes it. The container is configured entirely through environment variables instead
# (docker-compose.yml + .env), so the image is safe to push anywhere.
**/appsettings.json
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
**/secrets.json
media_storage/
**/media_storage/

# Not needed at build time
tests/
db/
docs/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/*.log
logs/
